synthesis.selection_rule_fix:
**What is replaced.** The registered best-arm rule, "most crop-years with skill > 0, ties by median skill", was used in v1 §7 and in v2-v5 §5. From v6 on it is replaced for every choice between models by the following.

**1. Score**
- **Primary: macro MSE skill.** S = (1/10) Σ_c [1 − Σ_{d,t∈W}(ŷ − y)² / Σ_{d,t∈W}(r − y)²].
  - All candidates are scored on the same district-crop-years against the same reference r, which is the incumbent's registered y_hist.
  - Squared error is pooled over the window W for each crop, and crops are weighted equally.
- **Co-primary.** Pooled district MAPE against actual Destatis yields.

**2. Decision (incumbent rule)**
The main model, now v4 F, is replaced only if the challenger passes all four conditions:
- it has higher S, with year-block bootstrap P(ΔS > 0) ≥ 0.95. Years are resampled with B = 10,000 and rng 0; seeds are resampled as well when each arm has at least 3;
- its MAPE is lower;
- no crop has higher SSE under the challenger in every assessed year;
- the evaluation years number at least 3, and none of them was used to design or select the challenger.

Otherwise the incumbent stays, and ties also go to the incumbent.

**3. Reported, never decisive**
- counts of crop-years with skill > 0;
- median crop-year skill;
- area-weighted MSE skill;
- total dt/ha SSE skill;
- squared-relative-error skill;
- the national, within-year and within-Land components;
- per-seed results.

**4. Not retroactive**
The H1-H13 verdicts and the v1-v5 selections stand as registered. An appendix re-scores them descriptively. Under proper metrics:
- v2 would have selected P or PN instead of D0;
- v5 would have selected F instead of PG;
- H10 (T vs A, Δ +0.111, P = 0.995) would pass.

Those changes are shown and not acted on.

**Why these choices**
- **The count rule rewards shrinkage.** For a forecast shrunk toward the baseline, b + λ(ŷ − b), crop-year skill > 0 exactly when 0 < λ < 2⟨y − b, ŷ − b⟩/‖ŷ − b‖². The count therefore increases as λ → 0: v4 F goes from 68/100 at λ = 1 to 85/100 at λ = 0.01, where macro skill is 0.004.
- **Squared error is the right score.** Pooled squared error per crop is proper for the conditional mean, and the models are trained for exactly that.
- **Why equal crop weights.** The benchmark consists of ten crop tasks whose yield scales differ tenfold. Area weights answer a different question, national production, and on 2016-2025 they happen to favour the gated arms: PG 0.200 vs F 0.185 against macro 0.143 vs 0.182. So area weighting is reported, and the fact that it changes the ranking is stated openly.
- **The rule is not uniformly stricter.** It is more powerful for large effects (H10) and more conservative for small ones. It must not be described as "stricter".
